# Local build + preview — fixed port 4175

When you **build and serve the production bundle locally**, use port **4175** on the loopback interface: **http://127.0.0.1:4175/** or **http://localhost:4175/** (same machine; `vite preview` uses `--host 0.0.0.0` so both resolve).

## Commands

- **`npm run deploy:local`** runs `npm run verify-env`, `npm run build`, then `vite preview --host 0.0.0.0 --port 4175 --strictPort`.
- This command must stay single-port and single-instance (no automatic fallback to other ports).

## What to do

1. Start or reuse preview at **`http://127.0.0.1:4175/`** (or **`http://localhost:4175/`**) only.
2. If port `4175` is occupied, stop the running preview instead of launching another instance.
3. When sharing a local deploy link, always use **`http://127.0.0.1:4175/`**.

See also `README.md` → **Local production preview**.
